>> On Fri, Aug 10, 2018 at 04:54:34PM -0700, rfc-editor@rfc-editor.org wrote=
:
>> A new Request for Comments is now available in online RFC libraries.
>>=20
>>=20
>>        RFC 8446
>>=20
>>        Title:      The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol=20
>>                    Version 1.3=20
>>        Author:     E. Rescorla
>>        Status:     Standards Track
>>        Stream:     IETF
>>        Date:       August 2018
>>        Mailbox:    ekr@rtfm.com
>>        Pages:      160
>>        Characters: 337736
>>        Obsoletes:  RFC 5077, RFC 5246, RFC 6961
>>        Updates:    RFC 5705, RFC 6066
>>=20
>>        I-D Tag:    draft-ietf-tls-tls13-28.txt
>>=20
>>        URL:        https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8446
>>=20
>>        DOI:        10.17487/RFC8446
>>=20
>> This document specifies version 1.3 of the Transport Layer Security
>> (TLS) protocol.  TLS allows client/server applications to communicate
>> over the Internet in a way that is designed to prevent eavesdropping,
>> tampering, and message forgery.
>>=20
>> This document updates RFCs 5705 and 6066, and obsoletes RFCs 5077,
>> 5246, and 6961.  This document also specifies new requirements for
>> TLS 1.2 implementations.
>>=20
>> This document is a product of the Transport Layer Security Working Group o=
f the IETF.
>>=20
>> This is now a Proposed Standard.
>>=20
>> STANDARDS TRACK: This document specifies an Internet Standards Track
>> protocol for the Internet community, and requests discussion and suggesti=
ons
>> for improvements.  Please refer to the current edition of the Official
>> Internet Protocol Standards (https://www.rfc-editor.org/standards) for th=
e=20
>> standardization state and status of this protocol.  Distribution of this=20=

>> memo is unlimited.
>>=20
